the clark county school district taking  now some proactive steps to keep  students and staff safe with a new alert  system victoria saha was able to get a  preview of this earlier today at mojave  high school she joins us now live  tonight here with more victoria  denise nine schools will be utilizing  this pilot program the school district  says their main focus right now are  those bigger high schools with multiple  entry points in case of an emergency  take a look at how it works  your crisis alert badge will work  anywhere on the school campus the system  is called essentials each staff member  will be wearing a land yard with a card  that has a button on it staff can click  on it to initiate a staff alert for  example if there was a fight in a  classroom it could also initiate a  campus-wide emergency lockdown if an  intruder were to build the building this  alert system works through wi-fi and  connects to a hub the hub then starts  activating strobe lights while alerting  campus emergency personnel  superintendent dr jesus jarrow wouldn't  go into detail on how much this is  costing but says he made it a priority  it's reallocating of dollars this is a  priority  our children and our staff need to be  safe we are prioritizing our existing  dollars  to make sure that our staff is safe ccsd  police lieutenant brian zing says his  team is ready to respond immediately for  an emergency and this new tool will be a  great resource to make sure every second  counts every year our officers go  through a very rigorous active assailant  active shooter type training it'll allow  our staff a quick and easy way to alert  us and district leadership that there's  an emergency at a campus after a school  year filled with violence dr jarrah is  hoping this tool will give everyone a  sense of safety next year what we are  looking at is what are the best options  for our students and for our staff we  are moving fast and furious  earlier this year an el dorado high  school teacher was brutally attacked by  a student that school has a different  pilot program that's audio based the  school district will then decide which  program they want to move forward with  reporting from mohave high school  victoria zaha live local now
 

